                  "explanation": "CAHIIM accreditation is the mandatory prerequisite for RHIT and RHIA exam eligibility. If a program loses accreditation, students who complete during that period may have their eligibility affected. AHIMA evaluates these situations individually, but the principle is clear: accreditation status at the time of completion matters. This is why AHIMA advises students to verify their program's current CAHIIM accreditation status. The most tempting wrong answer is 'automatically eligible' because it seems reasonable that completing the program should suffice, but accreditation is the gatekeeper.",
