                  "explanation": "The POMR was developed by Dr. Lawrence Weed in the 1960s. It has four components: database, problem list, initial plans, and progress notes using SOAP format (Subjective, Objective, Assessment, Plan). The POMR organizes all documentation around numbered patient problems, allowing interdisciplinary care teams to document under the same problem structure. Source-oriented (most tempting wrong answer) organizes by department, not by problem. Integrated organizes strictly chronologically. Hybrid mixes paper and electronic.",
