                  "type": "example",
                  "title": "Final Integration — Putting It All Together",
                  "content": "Let us return to Maria one final time and see the COMPLETE picture:\n\n**Registration (D6):** Maria registered, MRN assigned, insurance verified. The HIM department's staffing plan ensured adequate ED registration coverage. Budget allocated for registration system maintenance.\n\n**Clinical (D7):** Physician documented acute STEMI of the LAD. Troponin 8.2. PCI with DES performed. HIM professionals understand this clinical workflow to validate coding.\n\n**Documentation (D1):** H&P, procedure report, nursing notes, discharge summary all created in EHR using SNOMED CT, LOINC, RxNorm. Data quality checks ensure completeness. Legal health record defined.\n\n**Privacy (D2):** RBAC limits access. Audit trail logs every access. Maria's estranged family denied information without authorization. Encryption protects transmission to cardiologist.\n\n**Analytics (D3):** Door-to-balloon time tracked (met 90-min target). Case entered cardiac registry. CDS flagged troponin. Quality dashboard updated.\n\n**Revenue (D4):** Coded I21.01 (STEMI LAD) + PCI procedure codes. DRG 246 assigned. MCC captured. Claim submitted. Payment received.\n\n**Compliance (D5):** Coding audit confirms documentation supports DRG. EMTALA requirements met. Informed consent documented. False Claims Act compliance verified.\n\n**Technology (D8):** AI-assisted coding pre-coded the record. FHIR enabled data sharing with PCP. Telehealth scheduled for follow-up. ML model flagged Maria as high risk for readmission.\n\n**This is HIM. This is what you have learned. This is what you will do.**",
